      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 3.96,
          "en": "So let's now make sure we can listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.96,
          "end": 6.69,
          "en": "to a click on this delete button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.69,
          "end": 11.69,
          "en": "In Vanilla JavaScript, so in just JavaScript without React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.33,
          "end": 15.15,
          "en": "we would find a way of selecting this button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.15,
          "end": 18.96,
          "en": "for example, with document query selector button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.96,
          "end": 22.6,
          "en": "and then once we got hold of this DOM object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.6,
          "end": 26.72,
          "en": "we could add a click listener with, \"Add event listener.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.72,
          "end": 29.88,
          "en": "Now this is, again, an imperative approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.88,
          "end": 32.56,
          "en": "We describe what should happen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.56,
          "end": 35.83,
          "en": "With React, we rather use a declarative approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.83,
          "end": 38.26,
          "en": "describing the target result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.26,
          "end": 41.77,
          "en": "And hence, this is not code we write and React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.77,
          "end": 44.81,
          "en": "Instead with React, if we wanna listen to a click",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.81,
          "end": 49.81,
          "en": "on this button, we add an extra attribute on this button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.82,
          "end": 52.05,
          "en": "And for this, it's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.05,
          "end": 56.17,
          "en": "that all these default HTML elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.17,
          "end": 59.95,
          "en": "are, in the end, all the just React components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.95,
          "end": 64.39,
          "en": "just React components that are built into React already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.39,
          "end": 68.73,
          "en": "So they look like regular HTML elements and you use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.73,
          "end": 72.49,
          "en": "like regular HTML elements but under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.49,
          "end": 74.61,
          "en": "these are components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.61,
          "end": 77.63,
          "en": "And that matters because that means that you can add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.63,
          "end": 81.65,
          "en": "certain attributes which you could not add like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.65,
          "end": 85.03999999999999,
          "en": "at least with just HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.03999999999999,
          "end": 90.01,
          "en": "For example, on a button or actually on any HTML element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.01,
          "end": 93.9,
          "en": "here in JSX, you can add a on click attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.9,
          "end": 98.15,
          "en": "written like this, lower case o, upper case C,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.15,
          "end": 102.64,
          "en": "and the casing does matter unlike in regular HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 102.64,
          "end": 104.43299999999999,
          "en": "Here, it does matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 105.5,
          "end": 109.85,
          "en": "Now when you add the on click prop as it's called,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 109.85,
          "end": 113.7,
          "en": "as you learned, to a button or to any other element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 113.7,
          "end": 118.03999999999999,
          "en": "you're telling React that you wanna react to a click",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 118.03999999999999,
          "end": 120.16,
          "en": "on that element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 120.16,
          "end": 124.18,
          "en": "Now, the value you assign for this attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 124.18,
          "end": 128.17,
          "en": "is then not some text, not a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 128.17,
          "end": 130.69,
          "en": "but instead a dynamic expression",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 130.69,
          "end": 134.9,
          "en": "which should hold a function that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 134.9,
          "end": 136.97,
          "en": "when a click occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 136.97,
          "end": 140.22,
          "en": "So here, we could define an anonymous inline function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 140.22,
          "end": 144.47,
          "en": "like this or also with the arrow function syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 144.47,
          "end": 147.3,
          "en": "which you can use in Modern JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 147.3,
          "end": 152.3,
          "en": "or you point at another function and I'll do the latter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 152.91,
          "end": 157.19,
          "en": "I'll create a new function and important, I'll create it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 157.19,
          "end": 162.01,
          "en": "as a nested function inside of the to do function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 162.01,
          "end": 163.6,
          "en": "And that might look weird",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 163.6,
          "end": 166.52,
          "en": "but that's actually standard JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 166.52,
          "end": 171.3,
          "en": "In JavaScript, also without React, you can define functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 171.3,
          "end": 173.37,
          "en": "inside of functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 173.37,
          "end": 176.5,
          "en": "So here, I'll add a function inside of the to do function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 176.5,
          "end": 179.13,
          "en": "inside of that to do function component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 179.13,
          "end": 183.36,
          "en": "and we could name this, \"Delete handler.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 183.36,
          "end": 185.89,
          "en": "The function name is totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 185.89,
          "end": 189.75,
          "en": "I personally like this convention where functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 189.75,
          "end": 194.04,
          "en": "which are executed upon events, and with handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 194.04,
          "end": 195.67,
          "en": "but other people don't use that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 195.67,
          "end": 200.3,
          "en": "but instead might use, \"Handle delete\" or just \"Delete.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 200.3,
          "end": 204.17000000000002,
          "en": "Totally up to you, I'll go with, \"Delete handler\" here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 204.17000000000002,
          "end": 208.09,
          "en": "And then point at this function as a value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 208.09,
          "end": 210.21,
          "en": "for this on click prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 210.21,
          "end": 213.2,
          "en": "simply by repeating the function name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 213.2,
          "end": 216.5,
          "en": "And now here is an extremely important thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 216.5,
          "end": 218.26,
          "en": "to keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 218.26,
          "end": 223.26,
          "en": "You don't execute the function here so no parenthesis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 223.52,
          "end": 225.46,
          "en": "If you would execute it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 225.46,
          "end": 227.34,
          "en": "this function would be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 227.34,
          "end": 232.34,
          "en": "as soon as JavaScript and React evaluates this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 233.18,
          "end": 235.77,
          "en": "So when this line of code is evaluated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 235.77,
          "end": 237.96,
          "en": "the function would execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 237.96,
          "end": 240.07,
          "en": "Now that is too early though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 240.07,
          "end": 243.61,
          "en": "We wanna execute the function when the button is clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 243.61,
          "end": 247.27,
          "en": "not when that code is evaluated by JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 247.27,
          "end": 249.22,
          "en": "because that happens right before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 249.22,
          "end": 252.12,
          "en": "that content is rendered in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 252.12,
          "end": 254.77,
          "en": "Hence, we just point at this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 254.77,
          "end": 258.86,
          "en": "by just using its name here and that just tells React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 258.86,
          "end": 263.2,
          "en": "in the end that it's this function that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 263.2,
          "end": 265.123,
          "en": "when this element is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 266.14,
          "end": 268.68,
          "en": "And now in here, we can do whatever we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 268.68,
          "end": 273.57,
          "en": "For example, we can console log clicked here for the moment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 273.57,
          "end": 275.61,
          "en": "and if we do that and save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 275.61,
          "end": 279.28,
          "en": "if I go to the JavaScript console in the diff tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 279.28,
          "end": 281.97,
          "en": "if we click one of these delete buttons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 281.97,
          "end": 285.867,
          "en": "doesn't matter which one you click, you see, \"Clicked!\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 287.18,
          "end": 290.13,
          "en": "Now we could all the output, clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 290.13,
          "end": 294.64,
          "en": "and then as an extra log, \"Props.text\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 294.64,
          "end": 298.58,
          "en": "so that text value which we receive via props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 298.58,
          "end": 302.14,
          "en": "which has all the output down there in the h2 tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 302.14,
          "end": 304.76,
          "en": "I'm now referring to it again here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 304.76,
          "end": 308.09,
          "en": "because this is just standard JavaScript in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 308.09,
          "end": 311.81,
          "en": "even though this JSX code definitely doesn't look like it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 311.81,
          "end": 315.12,
          "en": "But up here, we write standard JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 315.12,
          "end": 316.2,
          "en": "and hence, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 316.2,
          "end": 319.42,
          "en": "here we can also use one of our arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 319.42,
          "end": 322.03,
          "en": "and if that argument turns out to be an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 322.03,
          "end": 326.12,
          "en": "which props is, we can also drill into that object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 326.12,
          "end": 328.73,
          "en": "With that, if I save this and click, \"Delete\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 328.73,
          "end": 333.23,
          "en": "you see the proper text being output here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 333.23,
          "end": 335.39,
          "en": "And maybe it's not clear here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 335.39,
          "end": 338.65,
          "en": "but that's another strength of React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 338.65,
          "end": 341.81,
          "en": "Without any extra work from our side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 341.81,
          "end": 346.71,
          "en": "these three different buttons are doing different things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 346.71,
          "end": 348.71,
          "en": "I mean, they're always doing the same thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 348.71,
          "end": 351.33,
          "en": "We just defined this logic once,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 351.33,
          "end": 354.46,
          "en": "but the concrete values with which they work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 354.46,
          "end": 356.63,
          "en": "the concrete text which they output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 356.63,
          "end": 357.83,
          "en": "is not the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 357.83,
          "end": 360.25,
          "en": "Instead, it's different for every button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 360.25,
          "end": 363.19,
          "en": "And that means that we can easily write logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 363.19,
          "end": 366.41,
          "en": "that's specific to a specific to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 366.41,
          "end": 369.72,
          "en": "whilst still being able to define this logic once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 369.72,
          "end": 372.1,
          "en": "instead of three times which is great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 372.1,
          "end": 374.483,
          "en": "and makes our code way more reusable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 375.58,
          "end": 378.28,
          "en": "But of course here, the goal is not to log something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 378.28,
          "end": 379.85,
          "en": "to the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 379.85,
          "end": 382.76,
          "en": "Instead, we wanna show a little overlay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 382.76,
          "end": 385.89,
          "en": "when that button is clicked and for this, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 385.89,
          "end": 389.2,
          "en": "we need to first of all create that overlay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 389.2,
          "end": 393.03,
          "en": "We need to create the HTML code that should be showing up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 393.03,
          "end": 395.35,
          "en": "and then as a second step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 395.35,
          "end": 398.693,
          "en": "we also need to find a way of showing it conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
